{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825406003,"sessionID":"ses_f461fdda8ffepr1o7xqEzpCNdg","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e8417e001TBl49dOtALBXgk","sessionID":"ses_f461fdda8ffepr1o7xqEzpCNdg","messageID":"msg_0b9e3e7bd0015IvMEQQVJ7pEUA","type":"text","text":"The instruction is clear. I've now read the full \"Background of the Merger\" (pp. 27–31, printed pages). Let me verify exact quotes against the source text and map them to printed pages before building the workbook.","time":{"start":1789825401214,"end":1789825406003}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825406050,"sessionID":"ses_f461fdda8ffepr1o7xqEzpCNdg","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e84290001nmNOsQuWzxWkO4","sessionID":"ses_f461fdda8ffepr1o7xqEzpCNdg","messageID":"msg_0b9e3e7bd0015IvMEQQVJ7pEUA","type":"tool","id":"call_00_ic6OGEyRYVMLr60jlmYj0459","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re, unicodedata\ntext = open('filing.txt', encoding='utf-8').read()\nlines = text.split('\\n')\n\n# normalize: join, collapse whitespace\nnorm = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text)\n\ndef find_line_ranges(q):\n    # find line indices containing parts - just locate via normalized index\n    idx = norm.find(q)\n    return idx\n\nquotes = [\n (\"A1\",\"During the meeting, Party A suggested possible joint venture arrangements and expressed some interest in acquiring equity in the Company to further develop strategic opportunities and enhance regional connectivity.\"),\n (\"A2\",\"the Board appointed a subcommittee of two independent directors, Frank W. Barrett and Richard W. Anderson, to interview potential investment bankers\"),\n (\"A3\",\"the subcommittee recommended to the Board that the Company retain GHF as its investment banking firm\"),\n (\"A4\",\"it was in the best interest of the Company and its shareholders to proceed with the transaction strategy discussed with representatives of GHF\"),\n (\"A5\",\"During the week of March 28, 2016, in accordance with the Transaction Committee’s directives, representatives of GHF contacted 11 potential strategic buyers (including Party A) and 18 potential financial buyers.\"),\n (\"A6\",\"representatives of GHF contacted 11 potential strategic buyers (including Party A)\"),\n (\"A7\",\"and 18 potential financial buyers\"),\n (\"A8\",\"the Company had also approached two additional Class I railroads to determine their interest in a possible transaction\"),\n (\"A9\",\"Each of the potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers subsequently executed confidentiality agreements\"),\n (\"A10\",\"and 14 potential financial buyers subsequently executed confidentiality agreements\"),\n (\"A11\",\"each potential buyer had been advised to submit a non-binding indication of interest by May 10, 2016\"),\n (\"A12\",\"which deadline was subsequently postponed to May 19, 2016 to ensure the potential buyers had sufficient time to formulate their most compelling offers\"),\n (\"A13\",\"Between May 19, 2016 and June 1, 2016, the Company received nine written indications of interest (“IOIs”) from potential buyers\"),\n (\"A14\",\"with offer prices per share ranging from $17.93 to $26.50 (assuming the conversion of preferred stock into common stock), implying equity values of $90 million to $134 million\"),\n (\"A15\",\"25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements with the Company and received information related to the Company\"),\n (\"A16\",\"the Transaction Committee concluded that the two low bidders should be excluded from that process\"),\n (\"A17\",\"The Transaction Committee authorized representatives of GHF to schedule in-person management presentations with the remaining seven potential buyers and allow these parties to conduct additional due diligence.\"),\n (\"A18\",\"representatives of GHF instructed all potential buyers to submit non-binding letters of intent (“LOIs”) by July 20, 2016\"),\n (\"A19\",\"In early July 2016, a potential strategic buyer that had not previously been part of the process (“Party C”) approached the Company’s management and expressed interest in acquiring the Company\"),\n (\"A20\",\"After executing a confidentiality agreement, Party C was provided the memorandum concerning the Company provided to the other potential buyers\"),\n (\"A21\",\"On July 12, 2016, Party C submitted an IOI with an offer price per share of $21.00 (implying an equity value of $108 million)\"),\n (\"A22\",\"Subsequently, Party C was provided access to the internet data site and the Company’s management held a management presentation with Party C by telephone on July 14, 2016\"),\n (\"A23\",\"In late July 2016, the Company received six LOIs with offer prices per share ranging from $19.20 to $24.00 (implying equity values of $96 million to $121 million)\"),\n (\"A24\",\"Party B submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $24.00 per share (subject to an expedited diligence review)\"),\n (\"A25\",\"Party E (a strategic buyer) submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $21.26 per share (subject to a 60-day exclusivity period for due diligence and negotiation of definitive documentation)\"),\n (\"A26\",\"Party D (a financial buyer) submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $21.00 per share (subject to a four-week diligence period)\"),\n (\"A27\",\"Party C submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $19.30 per share (subject to a 30-day diligence period)\"),\n (\"A28\",\"Party F (a strategic buyer) submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $19.20 per share (subject to a 30-day due diligence period)\"),\n (\"A29\",\"One strategic buyer and one financial buyer elected not to submit an LOI\"),\n (\"A30\",\"G&W submitted an LOI on July 21, 2016 to acquire the Company for a price of $21.15 per share (subject to a three-week exclusive diligence period)\"),\n (\"A31\",\"G&W submitted a revised LOI, which increased its offer to $22.15 per share (including $21.02 in cash and $1.13 CVR)\"),\n (\"A32\",\"The Transaction Committee concluded that the Company should proceed with confirmatory due diligence and negotiations with G&W and Party B\"),\n (\"A33\",\"representatives of GHF subsequently contacted the remaining bidders to inform them that they were no longer involved in the process\"),\n (\"A34\",\"During those calls, Party D and Party E both expressed interest in reengaging and enhancing their offers\"),\n (\"A35\",\"On August 1, 2016, Party D submitted a revised LOI at a price of $24.00 per share\"),\n (\"A36\",\"Party E submitted a revised LOI, along with financing support, from Party F, at a price of $23.81 per share\"),\n (\"A37\",\"Party D indicated that it would not proceed with further due diligence at that time\"),\n (\"A38\",\"Party E withdrew its revised proposal on August 2, 2016 (but confirmed its original proposal of $21.26 per share)\"),\n (\"A39\",\"the Transaction Committee directed the management team and representatives of each of BMO and Hinckley Allen to continue diligence and negotiations with both G&W and Party B\"),\n (\"A40\",\"the Transaction Committee directed representatives of BMO to inform G&W that the Company intended to enter into a merger agreement with another bidder\"),\n (\"A41\",\"G&W submitted a revised LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $25.00 per share in cash, which excluded the previously proposed CVR\"),\n (\"A42\",\"the Company and G&W executed the merger agreement, and the Company, G&W and the Eder Trusts executed the voting agreement\"),\n (\"A43\",\"Party B indicated that it would not increase its price\"),\n (\"A44\",\"The Company issued a press release publicly announcing the transaction on Monday, August 15, 2016 prior to the opening of trading of the Company’s common stock on the NASDAQ\"),\n]\nfor tag, q in quotes:\n    n = len(q.split())\n    idx = norm.find(q)\n    print(f\"{tag}: words={n:2d} found={'YES' if idx>=0 else 'NO '}\")\nEOF"},"output":"A1: words=29 found=YES\nA2: words=21 found=YES\nA3: words=16 found=YES\nA4: words=23 found=NO \nA5: words=30 found=YES\nA6: words=11 found=YES\nA7: words= 5 found=YES\nA8: words=18 found=YES\nA9: words=15 found=YES\nA10: words= 9 found=YES\nA11: words=17 found=YES\nA12: words=23 found=YES\nA13: words=20 found=YES\nA14: words=28 found=YES\nA15: words=17 found=YES\nA16: words=15 found=YES\nA17: words=27 found=YES\nA18: words=18 found=YES\nA19: words=30 found=YES\nA20: words=20 found=YES\nA21: words=24 found=YES\nA22: words=28 found=YES\nA23: words=28 found=YES\nA24: words=22 found=YES\nA25: words=33 found=YES\nA26: words=25 found=YES\nA27: words=22 found=YES\nA28: words=26 found=YES\nA29: words=13 found=YES\nA30: words=26 found=YES\nA31: words=20 found=YES\nA32: words=20 found=YES\nA33: words=20 found=YES\nA34: words=17 found=YES\nA35: words=17 found=YES\nA36: words=20 found=YES\nA37: words=15 found=YES\nA38: words=19 found=YES\nA39: words=27 found=YES\nA40: words=23 found=YES\nA41: words=24 found=YES\nA42: words=20 found=YES\nA43: words=10 found=YES\nA44: words=29 found=YES\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A1: words=29 found=YES\nA2: words=21 found=YES\nA3: words=16 found=YES\nA4: words=23 found=NO \nA5: words=30 found=YES\nA6: words=11 found=YES\nA7: words= 5 found=YES\nA8: words=18 found=YES\nA9: words=15 found=YES\nA10: words= 9 found=YES\nA11: words=17 found=YES\nA12: words=23 found=YES\nA13: words=20 found=YES\nA14: words=28 found=YES\nA15: words=17 found=YES\nA16: words=15 found=YES\nA17: words=27 found=YES\nA18: words=18 found=YES\nA19: words=30 found=YES\nA20: words=20 found=YES\nA21: words=24 found=YES\nA22: words=28 found=YES\nA23: words=28 found=YES\nA24: words=22 found=YES\nA25: words=33 found=YES\nA26: words=25 found=YES\nA27: words=22 found=YES\nA28: words=26 found=YES\nA29: words=13 found=YES\nA30: words=26 found=YES\nA31: words=20 found=YES\nA32: words=20 found=YES\nA33: words=20 found=YES\nA34: words=17 found=YES\nA35: words=17 found=YES\nA36: words=20 found=YES\nA37: words=15 found=YES\nA38: words=19 found=YES\nA39: words=27 found=YES\nA40: words=23 found=YES\nA41: words=24 found=YES\nA42: words=20 found=YES\nA43: words=10 found=YES\nA44: words=29 found=YES\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport re, unicodedata\\ntext = open('filing.txt', encoding='utf-8').read()\\nlines = text.split('\\\\n')\\n\\n# normalize: join, collapse whitespace\\nnorm = re.sub(r'\\\\s+', ' ', text)\\n\\ndef find_line_ranges(q):\\n    # find line indices containing parts - just locate via normalized index\\n    idx = norm.find(q)\\n    return idx\\n\\nquotes = [\\n (\\\"A1\\\",\\\"During the meeting, Party A suggested possible joint venture arrangements and expressed some interest in acquiring equity in the Company to further develop strategic opportunities and enhance regional connectivity.\\\"),\\n (\\\"A2\\\",\\\"the Board appointed a subcommittee of two independent directors, Frank W. Barrett and Richard W. Anderson, to interview potential investment bankers\\\"),\\n (\\\"A3\\\",\\\"the subcommittee recommended to the Board that the Company retain GHF as its investment banking firm\\\"),\\n (\\\"A4\\\",\\\"it was in the best interest of the Company and its shareholders to proceed with the transaction strategy discussed with representatives of GHF\\\"),\\n (\\\"A5\\\",\\\"During the week of March 28, 2016, in accordance with the Transaction Committee’s directives, representatives of GHF contacted 11 potential strategic buyers (including Party A) and 18 potential financial buyers.\\\"),\\n (\\\"A6\\\",\\\"representatives of GHF contacted 11 potential strategic buyers (including Party A)\\\"),\\n (\\\"A7\\\",\\\"and 18 potential financial buyers\\\"),\\n (\\\"A8\\\",\\\"the Company had also approached two additional Class I railroads to determine their interest in a possible transaction\\\"),\\n (\\\"A9\\\",\\\"Each of the potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers subsequently executed confidentiality agreements\\\"),\\n (\\\"A10\\\",\\\"and 14 potential financial buyers subsequently executed confidentiality agreements\\\"),\\n (\\\"A11\\\",\\\"each potential buyer had been advised to submit a non-binding indication of interest by May 10, 2016\\\"),\\n (\\\"A12\\\",\\\"which deadline was subsequently postponed to May 19, 2016 to ensure the potential buyers had sufficient time to formulate their most compelling offers\\\"),\\n (\\\"A13\\\",\\\"Between May 19, 2016 and June 1, 2016, the Company received nine written indications of interest (“IOIs”) from potential buyers\\\"),\\n (\\\"A14\\\",\\\"with offer prices per share ranging from $17.93 to $26.50 (assuming the conversion of preferred stock into common stock), implying equity values of $90 million to $134 million\\\"),\\n (\\\"A15\\\",\\\"25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements with the Company and received information related to the Company\\\"),\\n (\\\"A16\\\",\\\"the Transaction Committee concluded that the two low bidders should be excluded from that process\\\"),\\n (\\\"A17\\\",\\\"The Transaction Committee authorized representatives of GHF to schedule in-person management presentations with the remaining seven potential buyers and allow these parties to conduct additional due diligence.\\\"),\\n (\\\"A18\\\",\\\"representatives of GHF instructed all potential buyers to submit non-binding letters of intent (“LOIs”) by July 20, 2016\\\"),\\n (\\\"A19\\\",\\\"In early July 2016, a potential strategic buyer that had not previously been part of the process (“Party C”) approached the Company’s management and expressed interest in acquiring the Company\\\"),\\n (\\\"A20\\\",\\\"After executing a confidentiality agreement, Party C was provided the memorandum concerning the Company provided to the other potential buyers\\\"),\\n (\\\"A21\\\",\\\"On July 12, 2016, Party C submitted an IOI with an offer price per share of $21.00 (implying an equity value of $108 million)\\\"),\\n (\\\"A22\\\",\\\"Subsequently, Party C was provided access to the internet data site and the Company’s management held a management presentation with Party C by telephone on July 14, 2016\\\"),\\n (\\\"A23\\\",\\\"In late July 2016, the Company received six LOIs with offer prices per share ranging from $19.20 to $24.00 (implying equity values of $96 million to $121 million)\\\"),\\n (\\\"A24\\\",\\\"Party B submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $24.00 per share (subject to an expedited diligence review)\\\"),\\n (\\\"A25\\\",\\\"Party E (a strategic buyer) submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $21.26 per share (subject to a 60-day exclusivity period for due diligence and negotiation of definitive documentation)\\\"),\\n (\\\"A26\\\",\\\"Party D (a financial buyer) submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $21.00 per share (subject to a four-week diligence period)\\\"),\\n (\\\"A27\\\",\\\"Party C submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $19.30 per share (subject to a 30-day diligence period)\\\"),\\n (\\\"A28\\\",\\\"Party F (a strategic buyer) submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $19.20 per share (subject to a 30-day due diligence period)\\\"),\\n (\\\"A29\\\",\\\"One strategic buyer and one financial buyer elected not to submit an LOI\\\"),\\n (\\\"A30\\\",\\\"G&W submitted an LOI on July 21, 2016 to acquire the Company for a price of $21.15 per share (subject to a three-week exclusive diligence period)\\\"),\\n (\\\"A31\\\",\\\"G&W submitted a revised LOI, which increased its offer to $22.15 per share (including $21.02 in cash and $1.13 CVR)\\\"),\\n (\\\"A32\\\",\\\"The Transaction Committee concluded that the Company should proceed with confirmatory due diligence and negotiations with G&W and Party B\\\"),\\n (\\\"A33\\\",\\\"representatives of GHF subsequently contacted the remaining bidders to inform them that they were no longer involved in the process\\\"),\\n (\\\"A34\\\",\\\"During those calls, Party D and Party E both expressed interest in reengaging and enhancing their offers\\\"),\\n (\\\"A35\\\",\\\"On August 1, 2016, Party D submitted a revised LOI at a price of $24.00 per share\\\"),\\n (\\\"A36\\\",\\\"Party E submitted a revised LOI, along with financing support, from Party F, at a price of $23.81 per share\\\"),\\n (\\\"A37\\\",\\\"Party D indicated that it would not proceed with further due diligence at that time\\\"),\\n (\\\"A38\\\",\\\"Party E withdrew its revised proposal on August 2, 2016 (but confirmed its original proposal of $21.26 per share)\\\"),\\n (\\\"A39\\\",\\\"the Transaction Committee directed the management team and representatives of each of BMO and Hinckley Allen to continue diligence and negotiations with both G&W and Party B\\\"),\\n (\\\"A40\\\",\\\"the Transaction Committee directed representatives of BMO to inform G&W that the Company intended to enter into a merger agreement with another bidder\\\"),\\n (\\\"A41\\\",\\\"G&W submitted a revised LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $25.00 per share in cash, which excluded the previously proposed CVR\\\"),\\n (\\\"A42\\\",\\\"the Company and G&W executed the merger agreement, and the Company, G&W and the Eder Trusts executed the voting agreement\\\"),\\n (\\\"A43\\\",\\\"Party B indicated that it would not increase its price\\\"),\\n (\\\"A44\\\",\\\"The Company issued a press release publicly announcing the transaction on Monday, August 15, 2016 prior to the opening of trading of the Company’s common stock on the NASDAQ\\\"),\\n]\\nfor tag, q in quotes:\\n    n = len(q.split())\\n    idx = norm.find(q)\\n    print(f\\\"{tag}: words={n:2d} found={'YES' if idx>=0 else 'NO '}\\\")\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825401488,"end":1789825406050}}}}
